C# Classes and Methods Used
File.CreateText() – Creates a new text file.
StreamWriter – Writes data into a file.
StreamReader – Reads data from a file.
File.AppendText() – Adds new content to a file.
File.Delete() – Deletes a file.
File.Exists() – Checks if a file exists.
MessageBox.Show() – Displays a message.
Close() – Closes the application.
Clear() – Clears the TextBox.
System.IO – Provides file handling classes.
Project Description
This project is a File Handling Application developed using C# Windows Forms. It allows users to create, write, read, append, and delete text files. It also displays output messages and file content in a ListBox.
